<title>USA: PP&amp;L reduces power to 80 pct at Pa. nuke.</title>
<headline>PP&amp;L reduces power to 80 pct at Pa. nuke.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Power and Light Co said Thursday that power has been reduced to 80 percent at its 1,094 megawatt Susquehanna nuclear unit 2.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Berwick, Pa., was likely to resume full power later today, company spokesman Herb Woodeshick said.</p>
<p>&quot;They're doing work on the water tower. It's not a long-term problem,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The Susquehanna plant is joinly owned by PP&amp;L and Allegheny Electric Cooperative Inc.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
